      {"op":"not-claim","path":"/legal/agent/revoked","verdict":"FAIL","reason":"claim.revoked=true since 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z"},
      {"op":"delegate","target":"did:key:z6MkjNox...","verdict":"SKIPPED"}
    ],
    "short_circuit": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Resolvers MUST short-circuit on REVOCATION at any depth: a revoked delegation poisons all subtrees, even if other branches would have passed.",
    "This differs from cycle-detection (which guards against infinite recursion): revocation is a terminal condition that fails fast.",
    "Implementations should emit a structured event per evaluated node so auditors can reconstruct the full walk.",
    "The max-depth constraint on the innermost claim prevents unbounded recursion even when revocations are absent.",
    "Pair with patterns/claim-graph-resolver/src/cache.ts: a revocation event MUST invalidate any cached subtree rooted at the revoked principal."
